    "result_text": "All tests pass. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the soft-match \"possible duplicate\" rule for `POST /api/owners`. A new owner that clears the hard-duplicate check but shares an existing owner's **lastName + postcode** with a **different telephone** is still created, and now carries `possibleDuplicate: true` with `possibleDuplicateOf` set to the matching owner's id (earliest match if several); otherwise `possibleDuplicate: false`.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added persisted `possibleDuplicate` (Boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (Integer) fields with getters/setters.\n\n2. **`rest/function/owner/FlagPossibleDuplicate.java`** (new) \u2014 the pipeline step. It runs on the built owner, defaults both fields to false/null, then scans existing owners for a same-lastName (case-insensitive) + same-postcode match with a differing telephone, and flags it. A new owner without a postcode never soft-matches.\n\n3. **`officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted `flagPossibleDuplicate` between `flagBulkSignup` and `save`, under the write transaction.\n\n4. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf` to the `Owner` response schema so they surface in the generated `OwnerDto` (MapStruct maps them by name automatically; no mapper change needed).\n\n5. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the two columns; updated the positional `INSERT INTO owners VALUES` rows in `hsqldb/data.sql` (the DB the tests use) to match the new column count. h2/postgres inserts use explicit column lists and were unaffected; mysql has no owner seed inserts.\n\nTest result: `AcceptanceTest` (the soft-match checkpoint) and the full suite are green \u2014 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` / `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
